e  the actual house doesn't need as much  money as you thought spending on it as  possible but i'm very interested in this  deal i hope to see you man i hope to see  you soon hope so you do well  uh mr s says i've seen that most of the  birming most of birmingham's article 4  which makes finding a rent to rent  harder  i also tried contacting current hmo  listings on spare room and open rent  like you've shown us at the millionaire  intensive but no luck  are there other ways to find good hmo  deals and do you think there are enough  deals to go around people usually talk  about not having the funds but for the  deals i seem to that to be the  struggling part actually finding deals  firstly you correct that it is harder to  find the deals than to find the money  people say oh i haven't got any money i  can't get into property it's like hold  on even if i gave you a million pounds  tomorrow you wouldn't know what to do  with it let's get real so you're right  the biggest problem is not lack of money  it's lack of good deals that need money  so that being said by the way that's  some of you might be thinking about  having um  i'm having a go at you i'm saying you're  rubbish that's actually a good thing  because that means that you don't need  to find the money before you start  searching for the deal right now today  you could go start searching for the  deal and if the good deal comes the  money will follow it always does  so  listen in birmingham you can literally  go onto  the council website and see a list of  every single hmo in the entirety of  birmingham  so i think your problem is you've  probably not spoken to enough people  this is a numbers game and a skills game  you've got to speak to see more people  see more people see more people but also  don't say don't contact landlords and  agents and say do you do corporate let's  you got to go in with a story you've got  to go in and say hi this is my situation  this is what i'm looking for this is who  i am build rapport let them like you  people do business with people that they  know like and trust build rapport  tell me your story  and then ask them for the business  okay so good luck  all right mark coos  how do the real estate agents make their  commission if you do a rent to rent or a  lease option with the landlord why would  they be willing to put you in contact  with the landlord if they don't make a  commission  so  a lease option agreement  usually if they're listed with an agent  the agent can't sell the property  because the property is overpriced the  property's been on the market for five  years  and they can't sell it because it's  overpriced but the mortgage is so high  that they can't drop the price so the  agent's done with the property anyway  the agent's just like  whatever so you come on in  you don't even do it through the agent  you're gonna you're gonna contact the  landlord direct you can buy their title  deeds  on land registry for three pounds  contact them  direct and say hey i can see you  struggling to sell your house it's been  on the market for five years  i can see this in negative equity  you know what i'd like to make you an  offer which is like a rent to buy type  arrangement can we have a conversation  and then if they end up giving you the  deal a lease option agreement get the  deal then go back to the agent say to  the agent hey um i actually just secured  a lease option agreement on this  property i feel kind of bad um look can  i can i pay you your fee or something  and they'll be like well there's a lot  more where that came from you know  so i mean we're renting to rent they  will get paid they'll just get a small  percentage each month so it depends on  the deal but i hope that kind of answers  your question i hope to see you at the  crash course soon my friend awesome  will alexander says can you package and  sell deals as a teenager eg age 17 or  18.  um  yes  you can if you're 18 years old you're an  adult  you can do whatever you want  in england  uk you can get married  you can  travel the world you can set up a  business you can build an empire  do what you want  no different from a 28 year old  if you're 17 you are technically in the  uk you're a minor  so you can't set up a business bank as a  17 year old because you're a minor if  you're 16 17 you can't set up a business  bank  however you do have  a  national insurance number  you you should usually get a national  insurance number actually age 15 just  before you turn 16.  my videographer just told me that  information so thank you cara so when  you turn 16 if you've got a national  insurance number you can trade as a sole  trader and you can get paid so if you  want to help people you want to be a  deal sourcer  what i used to do when i was like 16  well 17 was i used to i worked as a sole  trader i used to find people tenants for  their rooms and just charge i was  getting paid for my time it's going to  be a deal source you can just say hey  can i go out on viewings and help find  you properties and you'll just get paid  by investors and landlords for your time  and then when you turn 18 and set up a  business you've now got a bit of money  behind you a bit of experience so yes  you can it's the is the simple answer  all right js says how do you systemize a  deal sourcing business and still earn a  grand fee from deals um you systemize it  by firstly you've got to focus on  actually making money packaging and  selling deals once you're packaging and  selling deals and you're making money  that's what you're just going to stop  bringing in staff  hiring  people to run the business for you  all right last question and then hey i  want to answer your questions so don't  forget comment below your questions  comment and comment and comment them and  i'll be answering them on the next q a  video so  abdelkansa says  what do you think about drop shipping  listen drop shipping as i don't know  lots about drop shipping i don't know 